 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Yes.** On advertised standard variable rates, investors pay about 0.58 percentage points more than owner-occupiers.\n\n- **September 2026:** investor 9.35% vs owner-occupier 8.77%, a gap of 0.58 points.\n- **January 2023:** investor 8.10% vs owner-occupier 7.52%, the same 0.58-point gap.\n\nThe gap has held at 0.58 points for the whole period since January 2023, even as both rates moved up and down with the cash rate.\n\nDiscounted variable rates, which most borrowers actually negotiate, show a smaller premium for investors. In September 2026 the investor discounted rate was 7.13% and the owner-occupier rate was 6.80%, a gap of 0.33 points.\n\nThese are advertised rates from the RBA's F5 table. The rates borrowers actually pay on new loans are lower and can differ from these, so the RBA's F6 table would be the place to check effective rates.",
